<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?><library hasTree="0" revision="R2024b"><block_node SID="25" hasTree="0"><block_name>Amplifier</block_name><block_class>rf.Amplifier</block_class><block_desc>This block provides four methods to model a nonlinear amplifier: Cubic polynomial, AM/AM - AM/PM, Saleh, and Modified Rapp.

The AM/AM - AM/PM model uses a lookup table to specify the amplifier power characteristics. Each row in the table expresses the relationship between power out or phase change as a function of power in.

The Cubic polynomial model uses the linear power gain to determine the linear coefficient of a third order polynomial and either IP3, P1dB or Psat to determine the third order coefficient of the polynomial.

The Saleh and Modified Rapp models are based on normalized nonlinear transfer functions. Use the Input and Output scaling parameters to adjust signal levels from their normalized values.</block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/Amplifier</block_path><block_open>$bdroot/Amplifier</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>0</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>195  130  265  200</block_position><block_icon>Amplifier.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>signal.in_signal:1,signal.out_signal:1</port_domains><block_type>MATLABSystem</block_type><block_reference></block_reference></block_node><block_node SID="22" hasTree="0"><block_name>Sparameters</block_name><block_class>rf.Sparameter</block_class><block_desc>Model an RF component described by a Touchstone file, an S-parameters object, or a Rational object</block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/Sparameters</block_path><block_open>$bdroot/Sparameters</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>0</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>330  130  400  200</block_position><block_icon>Sparameters.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>signal.in_signal:1,signal.out_signal:1</port_domains><block_type>MATLABSystem</block_type><block_reference></block_reference></block_node><block_node SID="11" hasTree="0"><block_name>Mixer</block_name><block_class>rf.Mixer</block_class><block_desc>Model a non-linear mixer with impairments. Impairments include a cubic polynomial non-linearity, I/Q gain and phase imbalance, mixer noise and profiled LO phase noise.</block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/Mixer</block_path><block_open>$bdroot/Mixer</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>0</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>125  240  195  310</block_position><block_icon>Mixer.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>signal.in_signal:1,signal.out_signal:1</port_domains><block_type>MATLABSystem</block_type><block_reference></block_reference></block_node><block_node SID="23" hasTree="0"><block_name>Filter</block_name><block_class>rf.Filter</block_class><block_desc>Model an 